  partName: Rear Blade Left
  description: The Rear Blade Left is a stationary blade located at the rear of the
    engine, playing a crucial role in directing the flow of gases and maintaining
    engine efficiency. Positioned on the left side of the engine, it works in conjunction
    with other rear blades to ensure a smooth flow of gases and minimize energy losses.
    Its shape and size are carefully optimized to maximize performance and minimize
    wear.
